{
  "id": "2026-10-25-uv-check",
  "title": "Python's fastest package manager now checks your code too",
  "topic": "테크",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Today's story is for anyone who writes Python.",
    "A company called Astral makes some popular Python tools.",
    "One is uv, a very fast package manager.",
    "Another is ty, a newer tool that checks the types in your code.",
    "Until now, you had to set them up and run them on their own.",
    "This month, Astral started to bring the two tools together.",
    "The idea is simple.",
    "uv knows which packages your project depends on.",
    "ty knows what your code actually does.",
    "When they share that knowledge, they can catch more mistakes.",
    "The main new piece is a command called uv check.",
    "It sets up the environment, installs what you need, and then runs the type checker.",
    "It also uses the same version of ty for everyone, so your laptop and your CI agree.",
    "Small scripts get help too.",
    "ty can read the packages listed at the top of a script and check it against them.",
    "For now, the feature is still experimental, so you have to turn it on yourself.",
    "Astral says it plans to make this the default later.",
    "If you have a Python project, it might be worth a try this week."
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "파이썬 도구사 Astral 이 패키지 매니저 uv 와 타입 체커 ty 를 묶는 실험 기능을 내놨다.",
    "새 명령 uv check 가 환경 준비·의존성 설치·타입 검사를 한 번에 하고, 팀 전체가 같은 ty 버전을 쓴다.",
    "스크립트 맨 위에 적은 패키지 목록으로도 검사한다. 아직 실험 단계라 직접 켜야 하고, 나중에 기본값으로 만들 계획이다."
  ],
